course: dictionary
lesson: 13659
title: Formal words: infliction
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to formal writing, such as history books, court reports and laws. They sound serious and often sum up a longer idea in one word. Infliction is one of them. It means the act of causing pain, harm or a punishment to someone.
explain: Use the clues around it. «The judge spoke about the infliction of a harsh punishment.» A judge deals with wrongdoing, and a harsh punishment is something bad, so infliction here means the act of giving that punishment.
explain: In everyday talk, people would say «causing harm» instead. Swap it in: «the causing of a harsh punishment» still makes sense, so you have found the meaning. Infliction is simply the formal way of saying it.
fact: Infliction is a noun, so you can say «an infliction» or «the infliction».
fact: «Infliction» means the act of causing pain, harm or a punishment to someone.
fact: «Infliction» can also mean something unpleasant that someone has to suffer, such as a long, hard winter.
fact: Formal writing uses words like «infliction» to sound precise and serious.
fact: A good check is to swap in «causing harm» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The king ordered the infliction of a harsh punishment.» What does infliction mean here? | *The act of causing a punishment | A long journey across the sea | A gift given to the people | A feast held in the great hall
exercise: «The long winter was a terrible infliction on the village.» What is the infliction? | *Something unpleasant the village had to suffer | A prize for the best garden | A new road built through the hills | A festival that brought everyone together
exercise: Which everyday phrase can replace infliction in «the infliction of pain»? | Feeling happy | Sleeping well | *Causing pain | Painting a picture
test: «Many people want an end to the infliction of harm on animals.» What does infliction mean in this sentence? | A kind helper | *The act of causing harm | A happy memory | A type of weather
test: What kind of word is infliction? | A verb, an action word | A prefix at the start of a word | An adjective, a describing word | *A noun, a naming word
exam: «The court heard how the infliction of pain had gone on for years.» What does infliction mean here? | *Causing pain or harm to someone | A kind of music | Building a strong wall | Feeling sorry for someone
